<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38809" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prō-mulsis</span></b> ,
		ĭdis, f.
		mulsum. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a relish</i> of eggs,
			salt fish, mead, etc., <i>served</i>
			
			<i>first at a Roman banquet</i>, <i>a
				whet</i>, <i>antepast</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				9, 16, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 20, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A foretaste</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libidinis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 24 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> For
			promulsidare, <i>the tray for the antepast</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Pall. 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
